	)
	(text_box "PCA9517A - I2C level-translating buffer (no rise-time accelerator). Isolates the RP2040 + slaves (A side) from the Raspberry Pi (B side). Chosen over the TCA4311A to avoid rise-time-accelerator/slave-ACK contention; uses static-offset buffering instead. Pi on B (offset) side, RP2040 + slaves on A (non-offset) side to preserve slave ACK noise margin. EN gated by ATtiny 3.3V GPIO, asserted 200ms after Pi power-on. B-side pull-ups to local 3.3V keep the Pi-side bus idle-high when the Pi is unplugged."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 113.03 17.02 0)
		(size 62.23 20.3053)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 229 191 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "7a592952-6e79-4e63-a4cc-17a3778491e5")
	)
	(text_box "We have 5 surface mount nuts for when using either a Raspberry Pi 3 or a Raspberry Pi Zero.\n\nRaspberry Pi 3:\n- 11mm J107, J109, J105\n\nRaspberry Pi Zero:\n- 12mm J108, J105, J109. These are for holding the Zero in place.\n- 9mm J107, J106. These are for holding the Sim/USB PCB in place."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 231.14 13.21 0)
		(size 52.07 26.4392)
		(margins 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525 0.9525)
		(stroke
			(width 0)
			(type solid)
		)
		(fill
			(type color)
			(color 255 229 191 1)
		)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "ed56295d-a0b1-41cd-874f-984e97848b81")
	)
